<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  #163 — the static contrast gate.

  Location: AGP reads the MODULE-level `app/lint.xml` automatically (a file at the
  repository root would be read by no module). Proven: the first `updateLintBaseline`
  run reported its `UnknownIssueId` finding at `app/lint.xml:15`, so this file is
  definitely the one being applied.

  TextContrast (text/background pairs below the WCAG floor) is declared as an ERROR,
  and it is deliberately absent from `lint-baseline.xml`: a baseline entry would
  silence exactly the class of defect this gate exists for. `XmlColorPolicyTest`
  asserts that invariant, so the baseline cannot grow a TextContrast entry unnoticed.

  KNOWN GAP — read this before trusting the line above: lint 32.1.1 (AGP 9.1.1)
  ships NO contrast detector (`lint-checks-32.1.1.jar` contains no `*Contrast*`
  class; `TextContrast` is reported as an unknown issue id). The declaration is
  therefore inert today and only takes effect once the toolchain carries the check
  again. The effective contrast gate in this repository is `XmlColorPolicyTest`
  (palette parity + `recording_*` pairs, both modes) together with the #161/#162
  audits. The `UnknownIssueId` ignore below exists solely so that this forward-
  looking declaration does not turn into a permanent lint config warning.
-->
<lint>
    <issue id="TextContrast" severity="error" />

    <issue id="UnknownIssueId">
        <ignore path="lint.xml" />
    </issue>

    <!--
      #187 — update notices are not defects and are never baselined.

      `NewerVersionAvailable`, `GradleDependency` and `AndroidGradlePluginVersion`
      compare against the live repositories, so their MESSAGE changes whenever an
      upstream version is published. A baseline entry therefore stops matching on its
      own (Gradle 9.9.1 → 9.9.2, robolectric 4.17 → 4.18.1 on 2026-11-22) and lint
      reports the entry as "fixed" while raising the same notice again as a new
      finding. Ignore the whole class here; a dependency upgrade stays a deliberate,
      manual decision.
    -->
    <issue id="NewerVersionAvailable" severity="ignore" />
    <issue id="GradleDependency" severity="ignore" />
    <issue id="AndroidGradlePluginVersion" severity="ignore" />

    <!--
      #196 — deliberate exceptions, documented instead of "fixed". Do not baseline
      these and do not remove the reasons: both are design decisions, not defects.

      `InsecureBaseConfiguration` — `res/xml/network_security_config.xml` keeps
      `<base-config cleartextTrafficPermitted="true" />` ON PURPOSE. Users point the
      app at arbitrary self-hosted endpoints (`http://10.8.0.16:11437/v1/`, Ollama or
      LM Studio on localhost), so a domain whitelist would break the core use case.
      This is the documented #114 decision — see `docs/ai/PITFALLS.md`, entry
      "Android 9+ blocks cleartext HTTP by default (#114)": do not regress to
      per-domain exceptions.

      `Overdraw` — the flagged root of `res/layout/ime_voice_input.xml` paints
      `@color/recording_overlay`, which is 90 % opaque BY DESIGN (`#E6FFFFFF` /
      `#E6000000`). Lint infers the shared activity theme
      `Theme.PolishedRecognition.Plain` (`res/values/themes.xml`), worn by the
      Workbench, Settings and Help activities; nulling its `windowBackground` would
      change or blank three activities, and giving the IME its own theme is a visual
      decision for the owner, not a lint tidy.
    -->
    <issue id="InsecureBaseConfiguration">
        <ignore path="src/main/res/xml/network_security_config.xml" />
    </issue>
    <issue id="Overdraw">
        <ignore path="src/main/res/layout/ime_voice_input.xml" />
    </issue>
</lint>
